 }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{(-2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{(2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=-5{x}^{-2},$ the lower bound is $a=-4,$ and the upper bound is $b=-2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{-2-(-4)}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(-4+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Develop