ue" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(\\frac{4j}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(\\frac{j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=-2$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+k\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/r