tion" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(\\frac{5k}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-{(-1+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=ln⁡(4x-3),$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-1}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+m\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(4(1+\\frac{5m}{n})-3)\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" 