ion-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(3+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=-1.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{3}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{n}=\\frac{b-(-1)}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=-1+\\frac{3k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=({x}_{k}+8{)}^{1/3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+8{)}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+8{)}^{1/3}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x+8)^{1/3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167" "basis" 312 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-73156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{e}^{3e}ln⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{e}^{3e}ln⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=ln⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=e,$ and the upper bound is $b=3e.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3e-e}{n}=\\frac{2e}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{3e}ln⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(e+i\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{4ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4e}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{(-2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{(2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[ln⁡(e+\\frac{2ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=-5{x}^{-2},$ the lower bound is $a=-4,$ and the upper bound is $b=-2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{-2-(-4)}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}-5{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(-4+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-2+\\frac{4j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(\\frac{4j}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(\\frac{j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[-5{(-4+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=-2$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+k\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2(5+\\frac{2k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(2+\\frac{k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(\\frac{5k}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-{(-1+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=ln⁡(4x-3),$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-1}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+m\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(4(1+\\frac{5m}{n})-3)\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[4(2+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(3+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-73185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=-1.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{3}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{n}=\\frac{b-(-1)}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=-1+\\frac{3k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=({x}_{k}+8{)}^{1/3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+8{)}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+8{)}^{1/3}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4739cd0ddc0c256dea2f977edee206b3ad8974a189eef4252ae55b77bd178f9a"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x+8)^{1/3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929463/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2e6346d752ba1e44954efae4a0af643c4d4fd5ff51f101d8fe611b55022167"} {"question" "q-346201" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/